### Batch ingestion (mix of eligible and ineligible users)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/batch-upgrade
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {"userId": "u100", "userName": "Alice", "age": 19, "balance": 120.50, "parentEmail": "alice.parent@example.com"},
  {"userId": "u101", "userName": "Bob",   "age": 23, "balance": 30,     "parentEmail": null},
  {"userId": "u102", "userName": "",      "age": 17, "balance": 12.75,  "parentEmail": "carl.parent@example.com"}
]

### Real-time ingestion (eligible)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/realtime-upgrade
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "u200", "userName": "Dana", "age": 21, "balance": 45.00, "parentEmail": "dana.parent@example.com"}

### Real-time ingestion (ineligible: age and balance)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/realtime-upgrade
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "u201", "userName": "Evan", "age": 25, "balance": 29.99}

### Idempotent real-time request: send it several times, it is processed and notified once
POST http://localhost:8080/api/realtime-upgrade
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-2026-0001

{"userId": "u300", "userName": "Ivy", "age": 21, "balance": 80, "parentEmail": "ivy.parent@example.com"}

### Operational metrics
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/upgrade.broker.pending

### Invalid request (400: missing userId, bad parentEmail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/realtime-upgrade
Content-Type: application/json

{"userName": "NoId", "age": 20, "balance": 50, "parentEmail": "not-an-email"}

### All processed requests
GET http://localhost:8080/api/processed-upgrades

### Filtered: ineligible only
GET http://localhost:8080/api/processed-upgrades?status=INELIGIBLE

### Filtered: one user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/processed-upgrades?userId=u100

### Simulated emails
GET http://localhost:8080/api/notifications
